implementationPlan.description:
ADVERSARIAL SELF-REVIEW, once, over this task's diff (load adversarial-self-review).

Destructive direction first. Can the new rule call a LIVE same-project daemon.json or daemon.lock a 'projectPath mismatch' where HEAD said same? Walk staleLockReason, validateDaemonInfoForProject, probeDaemonHealth and every deleter with:
- a relative --project ('.', 'sub/..') under a /mnt cwd (X9, X11);
- a Windows drive cwd, and a UNC cwd;
- drive-letter case and trailing separators;
- a file written by the other side.
Every changed verdict must be one of: POSIX case on win32, POSIX vs cwd drive on win32, a UNC spelling, a WSL share, or //x vs /x. Each must be either the intended fix or guarded by isForeignDaemonInfo.

Fail-open. List what now compares same that did not before. Two WSL distros that both have /home/u/p are the accepted exception, as in JetBrains. Can the proxy bridge to another project's daemon in any realistic layout?

Edge inputs: '', whitespace, '/', 'D:', 'D:x', '\x', '\\', '\\?\D:\x', a 64 KiB served path, U+00AD segments (JS compares code units, unlike PowerShell -eq), runs of '..', mixed separators.

Structure:
- No platform branch is left on the absolute route.
- The proxy and daemon algorithms are equivalent; step 4 proves both dists on one table.
- The comments name the contract's home and task-3def0804.

Rails:
- error handling: the rule never throws, and every child-process failure in the contract tests surfaces as a test failure;
- regression tests are present;
- no MCP contract change;
- existing daemon.json and lock files still parse;
- no forbidden pattern;
- the diff is at most 330 net.

planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
- Five implementations of the rule exist:
  - proxy utils.ts and the daemon index.ts twin, which compare only;
  - Kotlin DaemonIdentityProbe (WSL-share mapping, POSIX case kept, OS-independent);
  - the sh python comparable() and ps1 Get-MoeComparableProjectPath, which agree with Kotlin except on WSL shares;
  - scripts/local-runner/guest-session.mjs canonicalProjectPath. Its key names persisted VM ledger dirs, so it is left alone (noted on task-3def0804).
- VS Code task-80ed1fe8 was about to port the OLD rule. It now dependsOn this task and has a comment.
- On win32, only the TS rule sends absolute POSIX paths through path.resolve; that call is the whole DoD-1 bug.
- Live WSL seats run packages/moe-proxy/dist from this checkout (npm link), and the checkout's node_modules are Windows builds, so every build and test runs in snapshots.
